  .trailer-bg-wrapper {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    width: 150%;
    height: 150%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    pointer-events: none;
    z-index: 1;
    /*
      The video's edges — "no hard edges, even from the video".

      HORIZONTAL: this wrapper is 150% wide and centred, so it already spans
      -25%..125% of the info column: the video bleeds a quarter of a column
      LEFT, under the deck. The old two-stop ramp hit full opacity at 15% of
      the wrapper (x = -2.5% of the column), so the whole crossfade happened
      in a narrow band right at the seam and read as an edge. Full opacity at
      29% puts it at x = +18% of the column (-25 + 150 * 0.29), so the video
      dissolves in across a band ~43% of the column wide, straddling the seam
      instead of stopping at it.

      VERTICAL: the wrapper is also 150% TALL, i.e. it overhangs the panel by
      25% top and bottom. `.accordion-section` used to clip that off, but that
      clip had to go (hard rule 3 — it sat on the iframe's ancestor chain and
      iOS Safari renders a clipped cross-origin iframe as a black box). With
      the clip gone the overhang leaked the trailer down over the collapsed
      rows underneath.

