      the column boundary, so however soft the gradient was to the right of
      that line, the line itself was a step: pixel-scanning a horizontal
      slice across the seam showed a jump of 21-27 at x=756 on a 1440 render.
      A gradient cannot hide its own start — the fix is to move the start off
      the seam entirely.

      Sharing the video's box means the wash is already ~0.6 alpha and still
      falling by the time it crosses the boundary, and it keeps going into
      the deck column, where .deck-column's higher z-index paints it UNDER
      the cards — so it deepens the background the deck fades into rather
      than dimming the deck itself.
